<title>FRANCE: LVMH sales rise 4.6 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>LVMH sales rise 4.6 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>Turnover			31,140    vs   29,775</p>
<p>Note - Full name is LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton  </p>
<p>     - champagne and wines		     6,408    vs    5,836</p>
<p>     - cognac and spirits			4,884    vs    5,277</p>
<p>     - designer leather goods		  9,015    vs    7,415</p>
<p>     - perfumes and beauty products	  8,969    vs    9,277</p>
<p>     - other					 1,864    vs    1,970</p>
<p>It said in a statement that it expected higher sales and profits in 1997 before the impact of the acquisition of U.S. duty free chain DFS.</p>
<p>It said provisional sales for 1996 showed a 4.6 percent rise. Excluding the impact of foreign exchange movements, sales would have been 6.2 percent higher.</p>
<p>It said a drop in cognac sales, despite higher volumes, was due to weakness in Asian markets.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
